{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion","id":1409895,"title":"Thrown Confusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-23T07:21:22-07:00","id":1409895,"title":"Thrown Confusion","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I'm putting together a night caste that favors thrown as his combat ability and I'm curious as to how you have approached it in the past. I want to use Knives but it appears I would be much better suited to just take War Boomerangs as they are the only medium class thrown weapon and they have a bunch of useful tags. <br /> <br /> Is there a reason to take Chakrams or Knives over War Boomerangs? Am I missing some vital text that says I can't have 20 war boomerangs strapped to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:31:58-07:00","id":1409901,"title":"","content":"The main thing you get out of knives is that they're also melee weapons, chakram should by all rights enjoy a similar benefit but don't RAW for some reason (maybe because its use in melee is associated with martial arts? though that wouldn't explain the handling of the seven-section staff).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-23-2020, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:35:09-07:00","id":1409902,"title":"","content":"So, would it be out of the question to make &quot;Throwing Knives&quot; and remove the melee tag and put them in the same category as war boomerangs? Maybe add a piercing tag instead of melee or something to make up for the fact that they can't return to the character like boomerangs can?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:39:11-07:00","id":1409904,"title":"","content":"It probably wouldn't break anything, it really depends how much your ST cares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:59:33-07:00","id":1409909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion#post1409895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing some vital text that says I can't have 20 war boomerangs strapped to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you <i>could</i> do that, but try and do it IRL sometime. Now imagine walking around like that all day. Knives might not go as far, and may do less damage, but they're generally going to be smaller, meaning the number you can carry without it being obvious is greater.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Of course, even as I say this, the character I'm playing has three boomerangs on holsters on his belt.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T08:15:51-07:00","id":1409912,"title":"","content":"What about something like this:<br /> <br /> Light Class Throwing Knives,<br /> Tags: Lethal, Thrown (short), concealable, cutting<br /> <br /> Medium Class Throwing Knives,<br /> Tags: Lethal, Thrown (medium), cutting, piercing<br /> <br /> Edit: forgot to put Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 08-23-2020, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T08:36:03-07:00","id":1409916,"title":"","content":"Light weapons are also slightly more accurate than medium weapons, and knives are arguably easier to conceal. You can secret a few knives on your person and keep a boomerang as your reliable standby.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja\u2019d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T08:39:38-07:00","id":1409917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409916#post1409916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light weapons are also slightly more accurate than medium weapons</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in Thrown or Archery<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T08:40:38-07:00","id":1409919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409917#post1409917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in Thrown or Archery</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I\u2019m making all sorts of errors lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T14:33:10-07:00","id":1409963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409902#post1409902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would it be out of the question to make &quot;Throwing Knives&quot; and remove the melee tag and put them in the same category as war boomerangs? Maybe add a piercing tag instead of melee or something to make up for the fact that they can't return to the character like boomerangs can?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there'd be a mechanical problem with this, a medium throwing weapon named Throwing Knives wouldn't be a problem, but I'm struggling to imagine what it looks like in the fiction - Knives are light weapons because they're light, not because they're bad at being thrown. To make a throwing knife that's a medium weapon, it would need to be the size of a war boomerang.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't recommend piercing as a replacement for returning - returning is a solution to the problem of not being able to carry many at a time like shurikens or knives, it doesn't make each throw more effective in the way piercing does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T14:56:53-07:00","id":1409964,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, the weapons in 3e aren't even attempted to be balanced with each other despite the attempt to reduce this from 2e. The main options are to live with it (either building characters that will use the mechanically superior weapons for their combat style, or just accepting that you'll be doing slightly less damage, or have worse tags, or whatever), or doing a more comprehensive re-write (yes, fixing this one thing is worth doing if it's the only one that crops up in your game, but there's a lot of cases of weapons being objectively superior to other weapons in the book).<br /> <br /> There's a few older threads on ideas for addressing this, though I don't have links to them handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T14:57:36-07:00","id":1409965,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if I'm wrong here, but aren't throwing knives basically shuriken, or kunai? So what they have over the War Boomarang is that they're concealable and poisonable, which for a night caste assassin might be better than the added +2 damage.<br /> <br /> For example <a href=\"https://cdn.hiconsumption.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/09/Best-Throwing-Knives-0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">throwing knife</a>, vs <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/Kunai05.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">kunai</a>, vs <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/51xTt-2VZ8L._AC_SL1000_.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">actual dagger</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-23-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T15:17:58-07:00","id":1409966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409965#post1409965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if I'm wrong here, but aren't throwing knives basically shuriken, or kunai? So what they have over the War Boomarang is that they're concealable and poisonable, which for a night caste assassin might be better than the added +2 damage.<br /> <br /> For example <a href=\"https://cdn.hiconsumption.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/09/Best-Throwing-Knives-0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">throwing knife</a>, vs <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/Kunai05.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">kunai</a>, vs <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/51xTt-2VZ8L._AC_SL1000_.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">actual dagger</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it would probably just be easier to aesthetically change the shuriken to throwing knives and leave the stats as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T15:29:14-07:00","id":1409968,"title":"","content":"Throwing knives, like knives in general, come in a huge variety of shapes and styles. Kunai are just a specific style of throwing knife. That said, they're generally distinct from shuriken in that shuriken have multiple blades around a central axis to ensure one of them sticks in the target.<br /> <br /> The problem for the stat blocks, is that weapons like knives are Melee weapons with the Thrown tag, and don't have Tags that are specific to Thrown category weapons (like Concealable).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T16:04:20-07:00","id":1409971,"title":"","content":"If you all could flex your Ex3 might and help me with a few cool ideas I have for this night caste:<br /> <br /> First, are demon-blooded still a thing? This character's backstory is that he's the son of Sigereth, the Player of Games which as a mortal made him extremely lucky. He'd use this luck to out-con con-men and street hustlers and mobsters, etc out of their ill-gotten gains and turn the money over to outreach programs. He ends up Exalting as a night caste at some point during some dangerous heist I haven't conceived up yet. Because of his heritage, he has a distinct dark purple hair color and eyes that shine like gold coins in the firelight, and obviously the demon &quot;luck&quot; disappeared with his Exaltation. If anyone else has a cooler idea for a demon &quot;tell&quot; I'm all ears.<br /> <br /> He favors thrown, dodge, larceny, and athletics because of his natural luck and skill set. I'm looking at Sigereth, and she has 14 dice for &quot;gaming&quot; but it doesn't say what that dice pool is composed of. Would you guys assume it's larceny based?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Larceny as his Supernal but I'm open to the other three or something else if you all have a cool idea. I want him to be able to act like everything comes easy and natural to him. Flips, hitting bulleyes with his daggers, card games, all of it should look effortless and almost like magic (because it is).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":".  100th post, sweet 08-23-2020, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T16:45:05-07:00","id":1409974,"title":"","content":"IIRC demon-blooded are still a thing in 3e, but the implementation is likely going to be significantly different from 2e (though who knows how much/etc. at this point). If it's just cosmetic, it shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Gaming depends on what kind of game/character approach to it (one of the reasons why NPCs just get dice-pools for activities like that is to keep their stat blocks shorter and all). Traditionally in Exalted, War covers games where strategy is the most dominant component (like the setting specific Gateway), Lore for games where trivia/etc. is the most dominant component, and never really specifies for games of luck. Larceny vs. Investigation is generally appropriate for any game where the players are playing each other more than not (like high stakes poker players trying to bluff and counter-fluff) or cheating in general.<br /> <br /> Supernal matters for what Charms you want to get access to early. Most of what you're talking about is low level Exalted stuff, so it doesn't give a strong indication of what sort of Essence 3+ Charms you might want to get your hands on out of the gate to decide on a Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:10:21-07:00","id":1409977,"title":"","content":"For your Demon-Blooded I'd grab Larceny Charms like Swift Gambler's Eye and any Eclipse-Keyword Charms from Sigereth (I can't remember if she has any off the top of my head) or, lacking that, another appropriate spirit.<br /> <br /> \u200b(One of the Dragon-Blooded we've been given access to is not only Demon-Blooded, but has Charms that control the weather as a result of her demonic heritage.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:17:03-07:00","id":1409978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409974#post1409974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC demon-blooded are still a thing in 3e, but the implementation is likely going to be significantly different from 2e (though who knows how much/etc. at this point). If it's just cosmetic, it shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Gaming depends on what kind of game/character approach to it (one of the reasons why NPCs just get dice-pools for activities like that is to keep their stat blocks shorter and all). Traditionally in Exalted, War covers games where strategy is the most dominant component (like the setting specific Gateway), Lore for games where trivia/etc. is the most dominant component, and never really specifies for games of luck. Larceny vs. Investigation is generally appropriate for any game where the players are playing each other more than not (like high stakes poker players trying to bluff and counter-fluff) or cheating in general.<br /> <br /> Supernal matters for what Charms you want to get access to early. Most of what you're talking about is low level Exalted stuff, so it doesn't give a strong indication of what sort of Essence 3+ Charms you might want to get your hands on out of the gate to decide on a Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll try to run the gaming mechanics through with my ST and see if we can come up with anything. This is a good breakdown though. And yeah, I haven't really read up on too many high Essence charms in those trees, I was mostly just thinking of the thematics for my Supernal at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:18:11-07:00","id":1409980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409977#post1409977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For your Demon-Blooded I'd grab Larceny Charms like Swift Gambler's Eye and any Eclipse-Keyword Charms from Sigereth (I can't remember if she has any off the top of my head) or, lacking that, another appropriate spirit.<br /> <br /> \u200b(One of the Dragon-Blooded we've been given access to is not only Demon-Blooded, but has Charms that control the weather as a result of her demonic heritage.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which resource is this DB in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:39:12-07:00","id":1409984,"title":"","content":"That's Ledaal Kebok Coren, who has a minor blurb in p. 47 of What Fire Has Wrought, and a more substantial writeup in Heirs to the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T17:49:36-07:00","id":1409987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409984#post1409984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Ledaal Kebok Coren, who has a minor blurb in p. 47 of What Fire Has Wrought, and a more substantial writeup in Heirs to the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, thank you! I'll check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T18:14:17-07:00","id":1409991,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that also per Heirs, \u201cCan have unique Sigereth-inspired Charms\u201d is a five dot innate merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T02:43:49-07:00","id":1410028,"title":"","content":"One thing that I'd like to point out as someone who has played a Night with thrown as his attack skill. Thrown is great at opening with big decisive strikes but then really lacks in quality withering charms to help you build your initiative back up. So if you don't kill your foe/foes with that opening hit you are going to have to fall back on a different charm set to build back up for another decisive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T06:02:33-07:00","id":1410046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409901#post1409901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing you get out of knives is that they're also melee weapons, chakram should by all rights enjoy a similar benefit but don't RAW for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>A chakram has no grip. It's very thin and quite light. It is dangerous only by virtue of speed and spinning, though those qualities make it extremely dangerous. A real chakram is a metal aerobie with the sharpest edge possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T07:34:26-07:00","id":1410057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1410046#post1410046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A chakram has no grip. It's very thin and quite light. It is dangerous only by virtue of speed and spinning, though those qualities make it extremely dangerous. A real chakram is a metal aerobie with the sharpest edge possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">There were a number of variations on the chakram they came in different sizes, some had a grip and some were heavier than others. Suffice to say their value for potential hand-to-hand vs. being a thrown weapon varied accordingly.<br /> <br /> More </span>pertinently though<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">, this is a game which draws no distinction between knives and throwing knives. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-24-2020, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T09:13:40-07:00","id":1410084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1409991#post1409991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that also per Heirs, \u201cCan have unique Sigereth-inspired Charms\u201d is a five dot innate merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is very good to know.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looking at her charms, they all run around essence 6 lol. So, a 5 dot investment at CC might not be worth it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 08-24-2020, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T09:18:15-07:00","id":1410085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1410057#post1410057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> <br /> More </span>pertinently though<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">, this is a game which draws no distinction between knives and throwing knives. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm mostly just trying to give another medium thrown weapon option than giant boomerang. I think there's room in the weapon section for both knives and throwing knives.<br /> <br /> I think dropping the melee tag and bumping the damage is probably all that's needed. I think I can get my ST to allow for concealable as well. I probably could also just use Javelins or Short Spears I suppose. I guess I missed those when I was looking at medium weapons and only noticed Axes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T09:42:29-07:00","id":1410087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1410085#post1410085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm mostly just trying to give another medium thrown weapon option than giant boomerang. I think there's room in the weapon section for both knives and throwing knives.<br /> <br /> I think dropping the melee tag and bumping the damage is probably all that's needed. I think I can get my ST to allow for concealable as well. I probably could also just use Javelins or Short Spears I suppose. I guess I missed those when I was looking at medium weapons and only noticed Axes. </div> </div> </div> </div>Just my personal opinion, your ST can do what they want, but I don\u2019t think most medium thrown weapons should be concealable. <br /> <br /> Key to note here the concealable tag doesn\u2019t mean \u201ccan be concealed\u201d you can roll to conceal just about anything on your body, the concealable tag means that hiding them on your person is never more than a difficulty 1 roll. Concealable is for things like darts or needles that you can hide in your palm or hair or in your cuffs or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T09:53:47-07:00","id":1410089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1410087#post1410087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just my personal opinion, your ST can do what they want, but I don\u2019t think most medium thrown weapons should be concealable.<br /> <br /> Key to note here the concealable tag doesn\u2019t mean \u201ccan be concealed\u201d you can roll to conceal just about anything on your body, the concealable tag means that hiding them on your person is never more than a difficulty 1 roll. Concealable is for things like darts or needles that you can hide in your palm or hair or in your cuffs or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, fair enough. Yeah it's looking like Short Spears might just be the best option for a medium thrown weapon imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T10:05:03-07:00","id":1410091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1410084#post1410084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this is very good to know.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looking at her charms, they all run around essence 6 lol. So, a 5 dot investment at CC might not be worth it...</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s just why instead of lifting her Charms directly (which you also can\u2019t do because none of them are Eclipse Charms) you homebrew new Charms along similar thematic lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T10:29:20-07:00","id":1410097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1409895-thrown-confusion?p=1410091#post1410091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s just why instead of lifting her Charms directly (which you also can\u2019t do because none of them are Eclipse Charms) you homebrew new Charms along similar thematic lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or borrow from other splats and scrub the serial numbers off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"ht